# Lead-lens sign-off — cli#453 audit script
- date: 2026-10-26
- branch: docs/cli-453-coherence-audit-first-touch
- lead luminary: alan-cooper
- findings cleared: two, both caught during the read and both corrected
  before commit.
  1. A claimed finding that three skill descriptions show a unicode escape
     to the reader. A YAML parse showed the escape decodes to an em-dash.
     Dropped from the findings table and recorded under honest limits so
     the next reader does not re-raise it.
  2. The split-count table was derived by subtraction and read 9 and 11.
     Measured by running the script per group it is 7 and 9. Corrected,
     and the table now says it was measured.
- lens verdict: the audit answers the question a person would ask — can a
  new user read this — and ranks findings by whether a new user would stop
  reading. The two highest findings are structural rather than word-level,
  which is what the lens predicts when the word-list checks already pass.
- accepted gap carried forward: the script has no test. Stated in the
  pre-mortem ledger and in the audit, not hidden.
